---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import ClassRef from '../../components/ClassRef.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
import ApiTable from '../../components/ApiTable.astro';

const markup = `<div class="bo-combobox">
  <input class="bo-input" type="text" role="combobox" id="cb-input"
      aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cb-list" aria-autocomplete="list"
      autocomplete="off" placeholder="Search cost centers…" />
  <ul class="bo-combobox__listbox" id="cb-list" role="listbox" popover>
    <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="cb-opt-1" data-value="CC-1180">CC-1180 — Warehouse</li>
    <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="cb-opt-2" data-value="CC-2205">CC-2205 — Logistics</li>
    <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="cb-opt-3" data-value="CC-4021">CC-4021 — Procurement</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<script type="module">
  import { initCombobox } from "@busy-office/ui/js";
  initCombobox(); // once — filtering, arrow-key nav, Enter-to-commit, Esc/light-dismiss are already native
</script>`;
---
<Gallery title="Combobox">
  <p class="demo-note">
    A single-select text field that filters a list as you type — for picking one value
    out of a longer list than a plain <a href="/components/form">select</a> reads
    well, without the overhead of asking "which of these N do I want" up front. For
    picking <strong>several</strong> values, use the
    <a href="/components/dropdown">multi-select dropdown</a> instead — different job.
  </p>
  <ClassRef component="combobox" />

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Basic</h2>
    <div class="bo-combobox">
      <input class="bo-input" type="text" role="combobox" id="demo-cb-input"
          aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="demo-cb-list" aria-autocomplete="list"
          autocomplete="off" placeholder="Search cost centers…" />
      <ul class="bo-combobox__listbox" id="demo-cb-list" role="listbox" popover>
        <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="demo-cb-opt-1" data-value="CC-1180">CC-1180 — Warehouse</li>
        <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="demo-cb-opt-2" data-value="CC-2205">CC-2205 — Logistics</li>
        <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="demo-cb-opt-3" data-value="CC-4021">CC-4021 — Procurement</li>
        <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="demo-cb-opt-4" data-value="CC-3390">CC-3390 — Facilities</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Type to filter (case-insensitive substring match against
    each option's full text — try "log" or "cc-33"), <kbd>↓</kbd>/<kbd>↑</kbd> to move
    through the filtered results, <kbd>Enter</kbd> to commit. The listbox is a real
    <code>[popover]</code> — <kbd>Esc</kbd> and clicking outside close it without
    changing the field's value, for free.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>What the open list looks like — active option</h2>
    <div class="bo-combobox" style="max-inline-size: 20rem">
      <input class="bo-input" type="text" role="combobox" value="cc"
          aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="static-cb-list" aria-autocomplete="list"
          aria-activedescendant="static-opt-2" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Cost center (static snapshot)" readonly />
      <div class="bo-combobox__listbox" role="listbox" id="static-cb-list" style="position: static; margin-block-start: var(--bo-space-1)">
        <div class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="static-opt-1">CC-1180 — Warehouse</div>
        <div class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="static-opt-2" aria-selected="true">CC-2205 — Logistics</div>
        <div class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="static-opt-3">CC-4021 — Procurement</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">A static snapshot (no popover) so the
    <strong>active option</strong> styling is visible without interacting:
    <kbd>↓</kbd>/<kbd>↑</kbd> move <code>aria-selected</code> +
    <code>aria-activedescendant</code> down the filtered list — that's the
    highlighted row.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>No matches — the list closes, the field tells the story</h2>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">When the filter matches nothing, the behavior
    <strong>closes the listbox</strong> (<code>aria-expanded="false"</code>) rather
    than showing an empty popup — the typed text stays in the field. If "must match
    a known value" matters, validate on commit/submit: pair the field with the
    standard <a href="/components/form">error message</a> ("Unknown cost center")
    or the <a href="/patterns/validation-summary">validation summary</a> — don't
    invent an in-popup empty state the pattern doesn't have.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>In a filter bar — labeled, composed</h2>
    <form class="bo-filter-bar" role="search" aria-label="PO filters">
      <div class="bo-form-field">
        <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="fb-cb">Cost center</label>
        <div class="bo-combobox">
          <input class="bo-input" type="text" role="combobox" id="fb-cb"
              aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fb-cb-list" aria-autocomplete="list"
              autocomplete="off" placeholder="Type to search…" />
          <ul class="bo-combobox__listbox" id="fb-cb-list" role="listbox" popover>
            <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="fb-opt-1" data-value="CC-1180">CC-1180 — Warehouse</li>
            <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" id="fb-opt-2" data-value="CC-2205">CC-2205 — Logistics</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary" type="submit">Apply</button>
    </form>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">The real placement: inside a
    <a href="/components/filters">filter bar</a>, wrapped in a
    <code>.bo-form-field</code> with a proper <code>&lt;label for&gt;</code> —
    the combobox is a form control first.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>WAI-ARIA APG combobox pattern, not a custom widget</h2>
    <p>The input carries <code>role="combobox"</code>, <code>aria-expanded</code>,
    <code>aria-controls</code>, and <code>aria-autocomplete="list"</code>; the popup is
    a real <code>role="listbox"</code> with <code>role="option"</code> children.
    <code>initCombobox()</code> keeps <code>aria-activedescendant</code> in sync as the
    active option changes — nothing is simulated with generic <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>s.
    On commit, it fires <code>bo:combobox-select</code>
    (<code>detail: {'{'} value, text {'}'}</code>) — your code reads
    <code>e.detail.value</code> for the machine value (<code>data-value</code> on the
    chosen option) and persists it (a hidden input, a form submit, an <code>hx-patch</code>).</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Markup</h2>
    <pre><code>{markup}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { initCombobox } from '@busy-office/ui/js';
    initCombobox();
  </script>

  <ApiTable
    component="combobox"
    js="Required: initCombobox() — without it the field is a plain text input; typing does not filter or open the list."
    notes={[
      'Single-select only — the committed value lives in the input\'s text, not on any option (options never carry a persisted "chosen" marker across reopens). For choosing several values, use the <a href="/components/dropdown">multi-select dropdown</a> instead.',
      'The listbox is a native <code>[popover]</code> — never clipped by scrolling containers, and <kbd>Esc</kbd>/light-dismiss close it without touching the field value at no extra cost.',
      'Filtering is a case-insensitive substring match against each option\'s full text, computed client-side against the options already in the markup — for a server-driven / async result list, swap the options\' <code>hidden</code> state yourself in response to your own fetch instead of relying on the built-in filter.',
      'Commit dispatches <code>bo:combobox-select</code> with <code>{ value, text }</code> — <code>value</code> comes from the chosen option\'s <code>data-value</code> (falls back to its text if absent).',
    ]}
  />
  <Related links={[["/components/dropdown", "Dropdown"], ["/components/form", "Forms"], ["/concepts/accessibility", "Accessibility model"]]} />
</Gallery>
